      "node_id": "kg_doc_8",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Changshu () is a county-level city under the jurisdiction of Suzhou, Jiangsu province, and is part of the Yangtze River Delta. It borders the prefecture-level city of Nantong to the northeast across the Yangtze River. Due to the mild climate and terrain there, it has enjoyed a high level of agriculture civilization since ancient times, and is named after this, for the first character of its name (常 ) means \"always, often\", while the second (熟 ) means \"ripe\". The name of the adjacent county-level city of Taicang means \"great granary\".",
